<title>JAPAN: Japan end-April coffee stocks up 22.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan end-April coffee stocks up 22.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese warehouse coffee stocks totalled 67,298 tonnes at the end of April, up 22.7 percent from a year earlier, the Agriculture Ministry said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>At the end of April 1996, stocks in Japan, the world's third-biggest coffee consumer after the United States and Germany, were 54,836 tonnes, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Details of the coffee stocks were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Apr 97	  Mar 97	Apr 96</p>
<p> Brazil	     14,730	  14,187	10,481</p>
<p> Colombia	   13,227	  14,669	14,759</p>
<p> Indonesia	  11,213	  11,051	 8,334</p>
<p> Central America  14,422	  15,171	 9,307</p>
<p> Others	     13,706	  11,952	11,955</p>
<p> Total		67,298	  67,030	54,836</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
